Check out the AS/400 information on IBMs web site.  All processes
and all disk storage exist in a single 64-bit address space, and
the machine uses 128-bit pointers where 64-bits are used as an
offset and the remaining 64-bits contain information about the
object, which their web pages claim can be used to prevent illegal 
use of the pointer (this from):

