I had some Major Unpleasantness with a 6500 running NT4.0. Whenever I
would shut the system down (or whenever it would crash, which, this is
NT we're talking about, was quite frequently!) I would get an Operating
System Not Found message when I attempted to reboot.

I found it a mite tedious to use the handy Compaq Quick Restore CDROM
and reinstall all my apps each time the 6500 cratered.

The 6500 was remanded to the custody of Field Service. As it turned out,
there were two problems:

First, do **not** install Service Pack 4 on NT4.0. Stick with SP3.

Second, an examination under the hood (under the keyboard, actually)
revealed that the retainer lug that holds the hard drive in place was
not fully engaged. This may well have been the source of the OS Not
Found message.

One more issue. My 6500 has a DVD-ROM drive. The DVD-ROM has the
marginal utility of teats on a boarhog since NT4.0 does not have DVD-ROM
drivers.

