That is an old result for the R12000 (maybe in the Octane?).  
The current result for SPECint95 is 18.1 in a uniprocessor
system (Origin2000/300 MHz), or 18.4 if measured using only
1 cpu in a 2-cpu system (which is the smallest Origin2000
that we actually sell).

Although 18.4 is close to the bottom of the list (Power3 holds
that distinction), the range is so small that there is no way
that a person could actually distinguish among PowerPC, UltraSparc,
and MIPS without using a stopwatch.  The 550 MHz Xeon at 20% 
faster is probably about the minimum difference than an unaided
human could reliably detect, and the 21264 and PA-8500 are a
bit above that.

Of course, none of these systems run the same software, so 
making any sort of direct comparison experiment would be 
difficult.  It would be interesting to see how widely the
*compile times* varied across this set of machines -- that
would probably be much more strongly correlated with the
user's experience of "speed" than the SPECint95 scores....
