>*compile times* varied across this set of machines -- that
>would probably be much more strongly correlated with the
>user's experience of "speed" than the SPECint95 scores....

This gets back to the "system vs the CPU" arguments..  For
people not doing long computations, a system with a more
responsive UI experience is going to seem the fastest.  For
those users 10,000rpm disks, more memory and faster video
cards are going to be a better investment.  As for compiles,
if you have enough memory to keep all the compiler bits and
the file set cached, more processors are a major win.
Particularly in the PC space where you can put together
a dual processor box with half a gig of ECC RAM, dual
Ultra2 Wide SCSI channels, 10,000rpm disks and a 32MB
video card capable of doing (albeit not workstation
class) 3D at 1920x1200 with 16M colors and a 24" monitor
