: Kieran,
: 
: The DECservers (generally) use a command language where the commands work like
: this:
: 
: DEFINE - Modify the NVRAM settings but not the active.
: SET    - Modify the active settings but not the NVRAM
: CHANGE - Modify both the NVRAM and active settings.
: 
: When you log a port out, it reverts to the NVRAM settings.

Older DECservers did NOT have the CHANGE command.  So, you ended up typing the
same command twice: once with DEFINE and once with SET.

Of course, the DECserver 500 has its parameters stored on the load host, so it
really doesn't matter.  If you want the parameter to stick across terminal
server reboots, it needs to be set in the load image on the load host.

