In article <7i400o$c7t$1@autumn.news.rcn.net>, "Kenneth Randell" <kenr@datametrics.com> writes:
:I am looking to replace my aging DEC 3000-400 box.  I am told that I am
:budget poor (by my management), so I was looking at recommendations for a
:replacement system in the $2000-$3000 range, although perhaps this is
:unrealistic.  I have a handle on all of the different model lines, but it
:seems there is a lot of overlap in all of the Alphastation 500/600/800, PW
:433au, etc.

  Used?  AlphaStation 255 EV4 300 MHz series (the slowest of the systems 
  I've listed here), or AlphaStation 500 (EV5 266 or 333 MHz, EV56 400
  or 500 MHz) series, or AlphaStation 600 EV5 266 or EV5 333 series...

  The Personal Workstation series is another option, you will want to
  consider only the -au members of the series.  (I've more experience
  with the AlphaStation series than with the Personal Workstation, hence 
  the order listed here.)

  Remember to check the AlphaServer DS10 or AlphaStation VS10, as well...
  Either for purchase or -- with knowledge of the AlphaServer DS10 and
  AlphaStation VS10 prices -- to help you price out a reasonably speedy 
  EV56 box...

  PowerStorm 3D30 or better...  Dual-head it, if you can swing it...

  Systems here are capable of running multiple operating systems, as is 
  the PowerStorm 3D30 controller.  (Donno the official support status for 
  the other operating systems on the AlphaStation VS10, but all work and 
  are supported on the AlphaServer DS10 "twin".)

  OpenVMS version information: EV56 requires V6.2-1H3 or V7.1 or later, 
  Personal Workstation requires V7.1-1H1 or later, EV6 requires V7.1-2 or 
  (soon) V7.2-1 or later.  I do not know the Microsoft Windows NT or Tru64 
  UNIX version requirements for the processors off-hand -- though I do not 
  believe that the Windows NT support is quite ready for EV6.

  You'll need one disk for each operating system, and don't trust anything
  that wants to write anything claimed "harmless" to the disks of another 
  operating system...

 -------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
 Hoff (Stephen) Hoffman   OpenVMS Engineering   hoffman#xdelta.zko.dec.com




