Karland A Kilian wrote:
> 
> Hello,
> 
> I have a large Fortran program that I've compiled successfully using
> Digital Fortran on a DEC Alpha.  When I try to run the program, I
> receive the error
> 
> /sbin/loader: Fatal Error: Program datasize exceeds process datasize limit.
> 
> Any advice on what the process datasize is and how to change or check it
> is appreciated.
> 
> Sincerely,

You need to increase the data segment size. In the korn shell you can
see the limits with ulimit command. ulimit -Ha will show what you can
raise them to, then do a ulimit -d xxxxx where xxxxx is the number
listed against data(kbytes).

If there is still a problem then you will need to raise the maximum data
segment size in the kernel.

Nick Hill
UNIX System Admin



