> What makes the 575MHz 21264 slower than the 500MHz 264 on FP?
> Other motherboard? SMP overhead? Other cache?


The 500MHz DS20 uses the Tsunami crossbar switch chipset, while the
575MHz 8400 uses a bus-based backplane. The crossbar switch accounts for
a lot of the difference. What's more, the DS20 (and DS10 and ES40)
benchmarks used newer and better compilers.

