Mike Haertel (mike@ducky.net) wrote:

: I have no idea how the Palm Pilot port did it.

The m68knommu Linux port, as you suspected, only implements vfork.
vfork has the limitation that the parent process is blocked until the
child exits or execs, and the child must not return from the stack
frame whence vfork was called. You make an approximate copy of the
stack frame of the parent calling vfork at the top of the child's user
stack; returning onto this new stack with a 0 return value completes
the vfork. No base registers or segment copying required.

Keith



