In article <7hpli1$pr3$1@nnrp1.deja.com>, bob.edis@creatcomp.com writes:
:Does anyone know of any change in the behaviour of VMS mailboxes
:between version 5.5 and 7.2?

  OpenVMS VAX, obviously.  What processor?

  Given the amount of stuff that is dependent on mailboxes in OpenVMS and
  in application code, I would have expected to have seen at least a few 
  previous reports of any serious or general problems with mailboxes.  As 
  a result of this assumption, my initial suspicion would be a programming 
  bug somewhere in the application code.  

  I have found synchronization bugs are quite common, and can and often
  do lead to an application that appears to work fine for months or years,
  until <insert event> occurs.  Examples of these events include AUTOGEN,
  OpenVMS upgrades, ECO kit installations, upgrade to a faster processor,
  move from OpenVMS VAX to OpenVMS Alpha, upgrade to a multi-processor,
  etc.

  For information on synchronization problems to look for, search for
  "SMP" in the title of an article in the Ask The Wizards area:

    http://www.openvms.digital.com/wizard/ 

  Even though this may or may not be an SMP system, the basic requirements
  and general recommendations for synchronization are the same...

:A client has a system that was recently upgraded and now the mailboxes
:don't work.

  "The mailboxes don't work" isn't a particularly unique description of 
  the problem.  Additional information -- an example of the failing code, 
  the particular error message(s) received, the particular behaviour of 
  the application(s), etc. -- would be very useful in resolving this.
  With an example of the relevent source code, we can point out any of
  the obvious synchronization bugs (potentially) lurking in the code.

  Also useful would be a general description of the mailbox operations.
  (I've seen more than my share of bizzare and failure-prone application
  designs over the years, and also some really elegant designs... :-)

:I posted this to COMP.DEC.SYS as well so I'm sorry if you get it twice.

  Please consider specifying the two newsgroups in the headers, rather
  than making two separate postings...  (Also set up a follow-up group
  when you do this, so you don't have to search all the groups, and all
  the groups don't see all the resulting traffic... )  Thanks!

