Nick Michell wrote:

>                 440Mhz PA8500           500MHz 21264 w/4M L2
>                 N4000 - 1 CPU           ES40 - 1 CPU
> 
> SPECint95       base    peak            base    peak

> compress        29.1    36.3    <- !    19.9    22.9

Unless things have changed while I was away, this is due
to including data prefetching for the large array being
compressed.  Since most integer codes aren't helped by
prefetching, it's a peak rather than base option.

If you are using a PA8xxx, I strongly recommend giving
+Odataprefetch (sp?) a try.  When it helps, it helps
big.

