DSS/DW
	Using DB2 UD the E10K gets 57 x 1 CPU perf on a 64 CPU machine
	this was a full table scan on a 250GB table with 8 agregates. ~90%
	scalability.

	Oracle DSS four way joins 61 x 1 CPU perf on a 64 CPU machine. ~95%
	
	TMC Data mining 59 x 1 CPU perf on a 64 CPU machine. ~92%

OLAP using Holos
	54 x 1 CPU perf on a 64 CPU machine using 100 random
	queries from a Holos metacube. ~84%

SAP/SD
	32 to 64 CPU scalability factored for CPU performance shows
	90% scalability. The 32 CPU benchmark used 250 Mhz CPUs the
	64 CPU used 336 Mhz.

HPC scalability

Linpack
	Rmax and Rpeak virtually linear.
	16 CPU	64 CPU
	11.11 	43.82 ~99%
	12.85	51.2 ~99%

NAS 2.3 scalability averages 80x single CPU performance using 
64 CPUs when compared with 1 averaged across 24 benchmarks.
The worst scalability was 49x the best 144x.

I am not entirely sure what additional evidence you need 
though you may want more detail on the benchmarks run.

You can of course find examples of applications that 
do not scale at all or very poorly. Some because of System 
issues most because of application design. Lotus notes 4.5 
for example only scales to 4 CPU's due to the implementation 
of 4.5. Later versions of Notes do much better.

