: What's wrong with the existing open source OS's that use 64-bit address spaces
: on 64-bit hardware?  My understanding was that *BSD/Alpha does this.

"Wrong" is not the word I would use. The typical UNIX is rather far from a
single address space system. As in one can create a single address space
that has a number of cooperating services and applications within it, all
using fast rich communication mechanisms, with a reasonable degree of
security.

This is a different style of computing and one which I think is rather
attractive.

