>Furthermore, pointers can now be exchanged between processes in a meaningful
>manner.  SHM segments are now always mapped at the same address in each process
>which allows the use of actual data-structures in there.

You don't need to map the non-shared part of the process's address space
into the same VM area to get this benefit. In fact changing the mmap()
implementation (not even the documented semantics) so that if you don't
specify the mapping address you get the same address in every process should
provide the behaviour you're looking for.

