The graphics subsystem on the VAXstations don't do ANSI sequences, so you're
stuck with the console not being able to deal with them.

You can ask the system with an IF statement in your LOGIN.COM to see check
the terminal or line (I think it's OPA0:) and if it is the console to not do
the SET TERM/INQ to avoid the error.


i don't know what the hobyist license includes, but if it includes
DECwindows that's a way around the problems since the DECwindows terminal
emulators ARE  VTxxx compliant.


