Yes.

Sorry, seriously SAMBA maintains it's own password file completely separate
from the UNIX passwd system. On my machine this lives in 

/usr/local/samba/private/smbpasswd

There are some utilities (smbpasswd, addtosmbpass) which are used for
maintaining this file. There is also a mksmbpasswd.sh included in the
source distro for Samba which can be used to convert your UNIX passwd
file to smbpasswd.

I hope this helps

Paul


