Peter Mayne (Peter.Mayne@compaq.com) wrote:
: While there is no direct equivalent of kill -HUP in VMS, the original
: question also mentioned UCX & TCPWARE, which seems strange in the context of
: asking how to send signals to processes.
:
: Maybe the author, not knowing any better, and assuming that VMS works like
: UNIX, wasn't being specific enough, and was asking how to do the equivalent
: of kill -HUP `cat /var/run/named.pid`.
:
: In other words, if I have changed the DNS database, how do I tell the
: equivalent of the named process to reread the database?

Okay, given that specialized/modified question:

With TCPware, it's

  @TCPWARE:RESTART DNS

With UCX, I haven't yet found a way short of killing and restarting the
BIND server:

  $ @SYS$MAANGER:UCX$BIND_SHUTDOWN
  $ UCX ENABLE SERVICE BIND
  $ MCR UCX$NSLOOKUP some.host  ! to really start the process

cu,
  Martin
