If you can sucessfully implement your application on a large 
cluster of DS20's then do so. I didn't suggest that this is 
impractical for you. But it is for good % of the HPC market.

Many customers buy in apps rather than build their own. Unless 
their application vendor has decided to use MPI or a simular 
environment then they are going to be out of luck trying to 
run their HPC application on a cluster of small nodes.

> And why do you think it's so significant that Compaq doesn't release a
> new machine for every part of their product line the instant that a
> new CPU rolls out? That's the case for most computer companies;
