Subject: OpenVMS Shadowing Disk Geometry Restrictions Lifted
Date: 1999/05/06
Message-ID: <7gs81v$3g1@usenet.pa.dec.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 474748011
Distribution: world
Followup-To: comp.os.vms
Organization: Compaq Computer Corporation
Reply-To: hoffman@xdelta.zko.dec.nospam
Newsgroups: comp.os.vms,vmsnet.sysmgr,comp.sys.dec



  The requirement that all candidate shadowset members (that would be
  "disks", in English :-) have an identical disk geometry (numbers of 
  track and sectors, etc., must match across all disks in the shadowset) 
  has been lifted with the installation of the following ECO kits (and 
  later):

    xxxSHAD08_062
    xxxSHAD05_071

  Shadowset members are (currently and still) required to have the same 
  number of total blocks (LBNs).

  You must install the corresponding shadowing ECO kits across all systems 
  in an OpenVMS Cluster in order to use this capability.

  This change means that you can now create some "odd" configurations, 
  such as shadowing RAM disks or other pseudo disks with physical disks.  
  You can now also shadow any combination of physical disks or RAIDsets 
  that you can cooerce (or configure) into reporting the same total 
  capacity.

  No, I can't say when (or if) the LBN restriction will be removed.  There
  are a number of folks here in OpenVMS Engineering that would like to see
  that change happen, however...

 -------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
 Hoff (Stephen) Hoffman   OpenVMS Engineering   hoffman#xdelta.zko.dec.com




