Thats a bit hard to believe considering how agressive the 264 chip,
cache and memory system is.  I suspect what you might have heard
about the new Alpha RX.  

RX is basically an improvement in the old SX motherboard to support
faster L2 cache, faster memory system (75 Mhz 128 bit), and the improved
cpu.  The CPU is basically a 21164pc with some tweaks to the pipeline,
and a L1 cache thats twice as big.

Just the thing for people looking for a 64 bit cpu, alpha compatibility,
good FP or similiar.  

