|> Hi!
|> 
|> I got myself a DECstation 2100 a while back, and have been running NETBSD on
|> it.
|> However I'd like to get to know it's original OS. I believe it was running
|> ULTRIX originally,
|> but when I got it, it had no disk. Thus no OS.
|> 
|> Can anyone tell me about ULTRIX or whatever it ran back in the old days?
|> Is it possible to get hold of such an OS anymore?

Yes, it ran Ultrix.  I dont know if you'd want to get it anymore;
Ultrix is basically a 4.3-alpha derivative with lots of engineering
from DEC (SMP locking, DECnet, sun-licenced NFS under a `gnode'
layer).  No shared libraries. Bugs fixed in the final 4.3BSD release
(1986). Y2K bugs.

Unless you really need LAT or DECnet, NetBSD is probably a better bet--
and in many cases faster, too.



