monitor.  (Please note I'm not 100% sure about the numbers above - there is
someone in our office who has done some board-swapping...)  If the monitor
is a Digital product, and is a VRT19-HA, then you are definitely looking
at the high-res model (also possibly something like a VR320).  On the other
hand, if it is a VRT19-DA, or heaven forbid a VR290/299, then you're looking
at the low-res option.  I don't believe DEC ever offered a 19" SVGA monitor
in VLC days.

Over here, $175 would be about half the price of a spanking new 17" multi
sync model.  I would pay that for a 19" Trinitron model, but not for anything
less.  It's hard work getting a workstation (sync-on-green) monitor to work
on anything else - PCs, etc - so regard it as a dead-end.

