No Dave, the Alpha has the distinct dissadvantage of being relatively 
slow, at least for TPC-C and more expensive than either a Sun E450 
or a quad XEON. 

Of course the only benchmark apart from SPECint or SPECfp that 
you can use to make a comparision is TPC-C. On TPC-C the Alpha 
is the most expensive, the E450 is 50% less than the Alpha and 
a XEON comes in at 33% less than the Sun. Bot the Sun and the 
XEON based system are faster than the Alpha.

Factoring out the effect of the DBMS. Sybase and Oracle are 
30-40% less efficient than SQL-Server (but better at more 
complex queries) puts the E450 slightly ahead of the XEON 
but the Alpha is still dead last.

 
