Stuart Brook (sbrook@concentric.net) wrote:
: > Wondering what form factor hard drive I can use in my Multia.  I've
: > read that only laptop HD are able to fit, but a half-height looks as
: > though it may squeeze in.
: > 
: > Thanks..

There are two different hd mounting schemes in the multia. One is the
use of a 2.5" drive in the metal brackets toward the front of the 
machine and a 44? pin small ribbon cable to the smaller spacing
connector on the scsi card. This version leaves space for a PCI
card to be mounted inside the box and has an external scsi 2 connector. 
The second version has no PCI connector as it would block the 
installation of a 3.5 inch drive with a bracket that fits into the
slot where the pci bracket bolts in. This one uses a regular 50 pin
ribbon cable and has no external scsi port. I think the drives need
to be short (<1" tall) and low power, as the power supply in the box
won't handle a high performance drive.

: Well, someone just gave me a 3.5" scsi drive that came out of a Multia.

: Stuart

